silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_01_what_is_a_witness_concrete_anchor_3#joc620 silm:hasLongDescription "The joc620 is Witness joc620 is the fully assembled witness object at the end of the provenance chain: path=cannon/cat/joy_of_cats.md, lines=2340-2360, quote=\"Natural transformations from Hom(-,A) to a set-valued functor F are in natural bijection with elements of F(A)\", key=AdamekHerrlichStrecker1990JoyOfCats. All four fields present; witness is traceable and typed; its profile includes outgoing arrows to the Kleisli composition theorem." .
